### ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
### 🔐 ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES (Copy and fill in your secrets)
### ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

## 📺 YouTube Data API v3
## Purpose: Fast video metadata updates, view count tracking
## Get it: Google Cloud Console → YouTube Data API v3 → Create API Key
## Status: RECOMMENDED (fallback: yt-dlp direct scraping)
YOUTUBE_API_KEY=your_youtube_api_key_here

## 🛢️ Neon PostgreSQL (Cloud Database)
## Purpose: Remote backup, disaster recovery, cross-device sync
## Get it: https://neon.tech → Create project → Copy connection string
## Format: postgresql://user:password@host/dbname
## Status: OPTIONAL (local SQLite by default)
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host/dbname

## 📦 Kaggle API Token
## Purpose: Dataset versioning, reproducible backups
## Get it: kaggle.com → Settings → API → Create New Token (file: kaggle.json)
## Note: Token expires, rotate every 6 months
## Status: OPTIONAL (manual backup via db_exporter.py)
KAGGLE_USERNAME=your_kaggle_username
KAGGLE_KEY=your_kaggle_key

## 🌐 Google Drive (Optional for Cloud Sync)
## Purpose: Additional backup layer for critical snapshots
## Get it: Google Cloud Console → OAuth 2.0 credentials
## Status: FUTURE (not yet integrated)
GOOGLE_DRIVE_API_KEY=your_google_drive_api_key_here

## 📝 Flask Configuration
## Purpose: Development vs Production mode
## Values: development | production
## Status: OPTIONAL (defaults to development)
FLASK_ENV=development

## 🔐 Local Admin API Token
## Purpose: Protect admin actions, terminal, proposal inbox, feedback, and admin chat role
## Status: OPTIONAL in single-user local mode; REQUIRED before exposing app to others
NEWS_RESEARCH_ADMIN_TOKEN=replace_with_long_random_token

### ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
### ⚠️  SECURITY NOTES
### ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# 1. NEVER commit real secrets. This file is in .gitignore
# 2. Share .env.example only (with placeholders)
# 3. Rotate API keys every 3-6 months
# 4. Use minimal scopes (YouTube API: read-only, no upload)
# 5. For CI/CD: use GitHub Secrets or similar vault
